    <edge source="&quot;SIMULATION&quot;" target="&quot;CONTROL_STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">165.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Control structures (loops, conditionals) are necessary to implement the simulation of breaking bricks and checking adjacency."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control structures (loops/conditionals) are essential for implementing the step-by-step simulation logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Correct simulation of adjacent swaps depends on precise control structures to manage iterations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control logic is part of the simulation process to generate valid matrix values."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control structures (loops and conditionals) drive the simulation of subarray checks, but flawed logic in the control flow results in incorrect simulation outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The simulation relies on control structures to iterate and evaluate subarrays, yet the incorrect simulation logic highlights a misunderstanding of the required conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The simulation's accuracy is compromised by the incorrect loop condition in the control structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The incorrect loop structure in the code directly affects the simulation of palindrome checks, leading to an incorrect count of good arrays."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control structures (loops and conditionals) execute the simulation, but the flawed logic in the simulation causes errors."&lt;&lt;SEP&gt;"The control structures manage the simulation process, but the error shows the simulation logic is flawed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The simulation logic depends on control structures, but both contain errors affecting the solution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The simulation of matrix transformations relies on control structures (loops/conditions), but flaws in their implementation may disrupt the correct placement of elements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The simulation of matrix operations is implemented through nested loops and conditional logic to handle element swaps and position tracking."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control structures (loops/conditionals) drive the simulation of adjacent swaps to achieve the matrix transformation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The simulation relies on control structures (loops, conditionals) to manage swap operations and matrix state transitions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control structures form the backbone of the simulation process to manipulate the matrix."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control structures (loops/conditionals) are essential for simulating the step-by-step matrix transformation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nested loops in the code simulate the matrix transformation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control structures determine how the simulation of the 'X' attack pattern is implemented, particularly in handling edge cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control structures (loops and conditionals) are critical to implementing the simulation logic correctly, but the student's flawed control flow directly caused the incorrect simulation outcome."</data>
